-- title:
--   Order sum at a node place: length times branch rank bound
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring map $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, the integrality hypotheses on the two Hecke maps $\bar\alpha, \bar\beta$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$, with $k$ perfect. Let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, $w$ a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$, and write $B := R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ and $A_K := A \cap K$. Assume: node coordinates $c$ at $(K,w)$, so $c.x$ has zero residue on the first branch and order $1$ on the Frobenius twist of the second, and $c.y$ symmetrically; a nonzero $\varpi \in A_K$; $B$ local and Noetherian with maximal ideal $(\mathrm{nodeConst}\,\varpi, c.x, c.y)$; every $g \in B$ differs from some constant by a non-unit; the value integrality law for $w$; $w$ supersingular (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set); a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ with irreducible $\pi$, an integer $E \geq 1$, and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $B$ onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\pi^E) = W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^E)$ carrying $\mathrm{nodeConst}\,\varpi$ to $\mathrm{const}\,\pi$ and $c.x$ to $U$ times a unit $\alpha_U$; the height condition that any prime strictly below a non-maximal prime of $B$ is $\bot$; that every element of $\mathrm{fieldOver}\ (Nq)\ K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$; that $A_K$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$, together with a ring isomorphism $\tau$ from its adic completion onto $W$ sending $\varpi$ to $\pi$ and compatible with $\iota$ on constants. Finally let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $B$ containing no nonzero constant, $f \in \mathfrak q$ nonzero, and $S$ a finite set of places $V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ (Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$ and with evaluation kernel on $B$ exactly $\mathfrak q$. Then, in $\mathbb N_\infty$, $\sum_{V \in S} (\mathrm{ord}_V f)^+$ is at most the length of $(B/fB)_{\mathfrak q}$ over $B_{\mathfrak q}$ times the finite sum of $\dim_W (W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E))/Q$ over those primes $Q$ of $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ that are minimal over the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak q$ under $\iota$ composed with completion and do not contain $\mathrm{const}\,\pi$.
--
--   This is the per-kernel estimate in the count of zeros of a function at a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$: the places above the node with a given evaluation kernel $\mathfrak q$ contribute, in total order, at most the local multiplicity of $f$ at $\mathfrak q$ times the combined $W$-rank of the branches of the crossing model cut out by $\mathfrak q$ away from $\pi$. It feeds the total inequality at a node and the exact count of places with a given kernel.
